# CCO Microsoft Mail Ingestion Rules

CCO integrates Microsoft Outlook mail through Microsoft Graph.

## Core principle

Mail must be ingested once, stored once, deduplicated, processed through CCO filters and never reprocessed unnecessarily.

Do not build random component-level mail fetching.
All mail must go through the central ingestion pipeline in `src/ops/ccoMailIngestion/`.

## Source control

- Import one mailbox/account at a time.
- Each mailbox has its own sync state.
- Each folder has its own delta token/deltaLink in truth store.
- Do not delete mail from Microsoft during import.
- Reset only local CCO import state when starting from scratch.
- Keep import runs auditable.

## Microsoft Graph

- Use Microsoft Graph for mailbox access.
- Use delta query for incremental sync.
- Use change notifications/webhooks only as a trigger for sync.
- Use immutable IDs where available (`Prefer: IdType="ImmutableId"`).
- Store internetMessageId, conversationId and receivedDateTime.
- Handle throttling and Retry-After.
- Handle expired delta tokens by forcing a controlled resync.

## Idempotency

- Every raw message must have a dedupeKey.
- Every processing step must be idempotent.
- If a message is already processed with the same processorVersion and filterVersion, skip it.
- Reprocess only if explicitly requested or if filterVersion changes.
- Never create duplicate patients, duplicate tasks or duplicate timeline events from the same mail.

## Processing pipeline

Required steps:

1. fetch_from_graph
2. save_raw_message
3. save_attachments_metadata
4. deduplicate
5. security_filter
6. classify_mail_type
7. match_patient_or_entity
8. create_cco_action
9. audit
10. mark_completed

## Safety

- Do not send journal content or sensitive patient data to external AI.
- Do not auto-link uncertain patient matches.
- Do not auto-open/interpret risky attachments.
- Do not auto-reply externally without human approval.
- All patient-related mail must be traceable on the patient timeline.

## Performance

- Do not fetch all mail on every page load.
- UI must read from CCO mail tables, not directly from Microsoft Graph.
- Use background jobs for sync and processing.
- Use pagination and indexed queries.
- Cache read-only mailbox statistics where safe.

## Required UI

Build and maintain a Mail Ingestion Dashboard:

- mailbox selector
- sync status
- import run history
- queue status
- processed/skipped/failed counts
- needs review queue
- unmatched mail
- patient match suggestions
- failed jobs
- reprocess controls

Dashboard routes live under `/api/v1/cco/mail-ingestion/*`.
